  "description": "BOJYAE crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C65 H132 Co3 Dy3 N4 O28,H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.280-3.949 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.02-113.49°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C65H132Co3Dy3N4O28. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Co(III), Dy(III).",
